 "change": "OriginalObjectLoader.load gains rollback (default true, as before: a failed load leaves the loader unchanged). The loaded catalog moves its resources into each object loader and back (swap) and loads with rollback false: any error ends the catalog load, so no copy is kept, and each object's first Frame allocation no longer copies every earlier allocation (~15,000 by the end). Inside consume the sound registry and Frame heap move to the Frame loader and back instead of being copied. OriginalLoadingFiles checks a stream's mode and state through an in-place access instead of copying the Stream out twice per character or scanner access.",
 "profile": "A12 L13 load profile (shares of all game-process samples): OriginalFrameHeap.allocate's array copies (_consumeAndCreateNew 1.24%, retains 0.74%, element copies 0.43%), OriginalLoadingFiles.index 2.28% (Dictionary.Values getter and Stream destroy)",
 "review": "independent read-only reviewer: no bug (rollback true unchanged; rollback false gives the same object and state and leaves an empty loader on failure; nothing on the catalog path catches errors or reads the moved resources; the Frame loader gets the same values; index's errors unchanged); follow-ups applied before the gate: the comment no longer claims frame sound registrations stopped copying (they go through the Frame loader's own copy), the index comment, the test registration",
